      "items": [
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-001",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Negatively phrased stem. Item-writing guidance discourages 'NOT' stems because candidates misread them under time pressure, but the item is factually correct and has one defensible answer. A validator applying style rules flags it; one applying correctness rules passes it."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-002",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The keyed answer is correct only relative to the guideline supplied. Other major guidelines name a calcium channel blocker or an ACE inhibitor first for the same patient. The item is grounded in its passage but a validator judging against general medical knowledge will reasonably dispute the key."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-003",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The passage supports the key by inference rather than by restatement: it never uses the word prevalence. A grounding check that demands an explicit supporting sentence flags this; one that permits a single deductive step passes it."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-004",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Exactly-on-the-threshold values. The passage says 'greater than', so the key follows literally, but clinicians routinely treat borderline values as indeterminate and repeat them. Two reviewers can defensibly disagree."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-005",
          "verdict": "FLAGGED",
          "checks": [
            "structural/all_of_the_above"
          ],
          "why_edge": "'None of the above' is the correct key. A structural rule that rejects degenerate options flags this item automatically, yet the option is doing real clinical work here. Tests whether a validator's style rule can override a correct item."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-006",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The key is by far the longest option because the correct answer is a three-part protocol. A length-tell heuristic fires; the length is justified by the content. Tests whether the validator distinguishes a cue from a fact."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-007",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Nationally and temporally specific. The key is correct for the programme quoted and wrong elsewhere, and national protocols are revised. A validator with a general medical prior will often dispute it."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-008",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Two options are on the same causal chain: increased sympathetic outflow causes the increased heart rate. 'First' resolves it in favour of the key, but a reviewer may call the pair insufficiently distinct."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-009",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Three options rather than four. The structural minimum permits three, but a house style requiring four options would reject it. Also tests whether the validator notices that the passage itself acknowledges an alternative formula."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-010",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The assertion-reason format deliberately contains a non-explanatory true reason. A validator checking 'does the explanation support the key' may read the non-sequitur as the defect 'poor_reasoning' when it is the format working as intended."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-011",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The explanation is a four-word clause. It is not wrong and the key is correct, but it explains nothing. Whether a thin explanation constitutes a defect is a policy question, not a factual one."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-012",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The reference given for this item names a standard textbook at book level with no edition, page or chapter. That is not a fabricated citation, but it is not a checkable one either. Whether an uncheckable reference is a defect is a policy question."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-013",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The vignette omits vital signs, weight and past history. The answer is nonetheless determined by the features given. A validator that requires a complete data set in a vignette flags it as under-specified; one that asks only whether the answer follows passes it."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-014",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Arithmetic that a validator must actually perform to check. Layer A cannot do it and a judge that estimates rather than calculates will often get it wrong in either direction. Included to measure where numerical checking fails, not to be scored."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-015",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The item uses the international non-proprietary spelling 'meticillin' while most Indian textbooks and candidates use 'methicillin'. A validator matching against a term list may treat the spelling as an error; it is not one."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-016",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The key is a limit age and a distractor, 15 months, falls inside the normal range given in the passage. Ranges that overlap options make the key defensible rather than uniquely correct."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-017",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Screening intervals differ between national programmes and change as programmes migrate to HPV primary testing. The key is grounded in the passage and contradicted by other real programmes."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-018",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The passage contains a unit error in its final sentence: pressure is not measured per litre. The key does not depend on that sentence. Whether a flaw in the evidence that does not affect the answer makes the item defective is a policy question."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-019",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "Pure recall of a classification, but the item is declared at foundation difficulty, where recall is the intended level. Included to check that a validator's 'trivial' rule reads the declared difficulty rather than firing on recall alone."
        },
        {
          "id": "vd-edge-020",
          "verdict": "PASSED",
          "checks": [],
          "why_edge": "The ranking depends on the dataset, the period and whether indirect causes are counted. The passage supports the key; published sources for other populations and periods support the second option. Reviewers with different sources will key it differently."
        }
      ]
    },
